<blockquote>
<p>probably make sense overall as far as modern science can tell, unless there's mind control</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The article states:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Once in the bloodstream, instances grow from less than a millimeter in diameter to many times their original size, the largest recorded specimen being 2.1&#160;cm in diameter</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm not sure how many parasites can do that in a host's bloodstream. Granted, there's no timeframe given, but there are other small things about this fish that don't strike me as easily explained by studies done on other parasites.</p>
<p>Personally, I like it because it sort of tiptoes on the edge between anomaly and potential reality.</p>

